Ngā Tī Kōuka Puāwai
2026-10-23

{Verse 1}
Little trees with white leaves
Burst from little flaxes
As they reach sunward
Atop crooked spines,
Cheating past shrubs and vines.

{Verse 2}
The flies are less sure
Of what to reach for.
Content, perhaps, just to add their buzz
To the gentle sounds
Of a summer that's not quite here.

{Verse 3}
O those blessed sounds:
The kōtare and the warbler,
Bold tūī high in kānuka,
The rustle of the cool wind
As it fights the beautiful, burning sun.

{Bridge}
Here's my gold, my gift from heaven.
Here's my soul, it is abundant.

{Coda}
A rich man, here I sit,
Freed from true deficit,
Breathing in rest exotic,
Knowing just one thought is fit:

God is good.

{Outro}
God is good.

